  "scope": "Exact cumulative V3 frozen52 plus worker7 retained pattern plans and worker14 reference header/common pure DB memo/accounting plus root4 production pattern routing/public types and retained BodyIndex range lookup. Replaces production per-phase full pattern/header planning with existing dependency-tracked queries; checked immutable Arc pins, actual source authority and separate reached namespace/runtime proofs. Includes unchanged326case512file upstream inventory. Source-only/uncompiled/unexecuted, no task/architecture/upstream/JIT acceptance. Earlier V3 preserved unexecuted.",
  "architecture_review": {
    "1_to_4": "Ordinary query/source/type and verifier/VM routes; public types are opaque plans, not execution authority. No new assertion/expression/macro/method/numeric engine or generated-source-only rule.",
    "5": "Common retained pattern rows and transaction operations; root production fallback refuses source-plan reconstruction. Existing boolean-match-guard admission remains in one-time preparation. Structural/non-Copy/ref/let-else and applicable macro matrix remain incomplete.",
    "6": "Pure PatternPlan(owner Entry PcKey) and ReferenceHeader(definition) queries use actual tracked source/body/signature/parse dependencies. Parameter/result and phase selection borrow shared immutable plans. Test-only ephemeral adapters use the same plan constructors/lowerers. Obsolete direct scalar binding wrapper and reference reconstruction methods deleted.",
    "7": "Namespace and runtime ticket certificates remain separate reached authority. Existing census/unrelated invalidation debt remains open; source plan keys introduce no whole-world map.",
    "8": "Arc shared parser/body roots are charged/deduplicated through retained plan lifetime and eviction. Root nodes_at_range uses derived sorted NodeIds with checked storage, preserves all equal-range IDs and original first-role match; one O(n log n) index build, O(log n + equal-range candidates) lookup. New index rows are derived from explicitly encoded semantic nodes and not a second source identity. No performance measurement or acceptance claim."
  },
